  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nForecast Remains on Track: \n\nThe forecast is very straight-forward through the next week, and \nconfidence is therefore high in the forecast details. Global model\nensembles agree that an anomalously warm upper level ridge will \nslowly shift eastward across the lower Mississippi Valley region \nas we finish up the week and go into next week. This will lead to \na continuation of dry weather with large diurnal temperature \nranges approaching 40 deg F. \n\nOf greatest importance, the continued drying of vegetation \ncombined with exceptionally low daytime RH values will help to \nmaintain an elevated fire danger threat. We will continue to \nmessage this through the graphics and fire danger statement. Wind \nshould have less influence and be a smaller factor in determining \nthe fire danger threat levels. \n\nOtherwise, rainfall is not expected until late next week at the \nearliest, when the ridge shows signs of breaking down. /EC/OAJ/",
